  "description": "SABTAV crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group C 2. Reported CIF formula moiety: C88 H152 Cu8 Dy4 N4 O44,4.5(C1 H4 O1),4(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Dy1 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy3 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy4 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Cu1 (Cu) has 6 O neighbors; Cu2 (Cu) has 4 O neighbors; Cu3 (Cu) has 4 O neighbors; Cu4 (Cu) has 6 O neighbors; Cu5 (Cu) has 6 O neighbors; Cu6 (Cu) has 4 O neighbors; Cu7 (Cu) has 4 O neighbors; Cu8 (Cu) has 6 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 24 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.182-3.993 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 93.70-115.09°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C88H152Cu8Dy4N4O44·4.5MeOH·4H2O. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 8 OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 4 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
